34,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found that the community halls kept their evening timetables despite the road closures. That is really encouraging!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The digitisation batch left half its images unindexed. The partner groups, however, still meet unaided. The records were never properly closed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The register shows retired tradespeople running the clinic, but no paid staff can supervise them. That is a critical gap.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The grant covers sessions for twelve months, then the flat budget absorbs them. The vehicle line overran by a third. That is where the thinness begins.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The bus cuts are severe. An hour round trip means the outer wards are effectively locked out.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that is tough. But the halls kept their own schedules! I think community-led sessions might be the key to staying open.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shion, that supervision gap explains why the partner groups survived. They didn’t need our oversight, just a room.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, exactly. They bypassed the bottleneck. I need to know if we can replicate that model without hiring new supervisors.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle overrun is the real trap. Once the grant expires, that recurring cost hits the flat budget hard.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, the halls staying open is good, but the bus cuts mean our branches are still out of reach for many.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I see! If the partner groups survive without us, maybe we should just support them. It feels safer than relying on our own fragile timetables.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, precisely. The partner groups proved the demand exists without our overhead. We should stop reinventing the wheel and just fund the room.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Yumi, supporting them is smart, but only if we stop pretending we can manage them. The roster simply does not have the capacity for new supervision.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, agreed. The roster gap is real. But the funding structure is the deeper issue. We cannot absorb recurring costs after the grant ends.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, the funding gap is real. But the evening data shows people are already there, just after we lock up.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that is a great insight! If people are already there in the evenings, we just need to open the doors. It feels much more reliable than fighting the weather.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Daisuke, the attendance sheets confirm it. Forty visitors per session in the outer wards. We ignored that data for six years.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, evening demand is real, but it requires staff who are not there. We cannot open doors without bodies to run them.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, the evening demand is real, but the vehicle overrun means we cannot sustain the extra hours. The funding structure simply does not support it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, I hear you. But the remote catalogue peaks after nine. Maybe we can extend hours without full staffing?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
